id: pm-github-refused-close-attribution
title: Preserve the attempted PR in published closeout refusals
description: The closeout review artifact can name an earlier candidate when an explicit delivery tag selects a different PR and policy refuses the close.
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: closeout
created_at: "2026-11-24T06:45:18.774Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T07:00:34.419Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A refused delivery selected explicitly from two candidates names the attempted PR and preserves candidate and missing evidence. A single-candidate refusal keeps its original PR.
repro_steps: "Give one item merged candidates 42 and 43, select 43 using delivery-pr, and require an absent field on close. Run the workflow fixture and inspect closeout-review.json."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T06:45:30.937Z",codex-agent,Follow-up to pm-github-jx5q for review thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM67Jdvs. The candidate rows should keep their original identities. The workflow projection will use the attempted PR recorded in close_refused evidence and retain the candidate list before deduplication.
  "2026-11-24T07:00:24.118Z",codex-agent,"The review artifact derives pr from close_refused evidence before deduplicating by item, and retains candidates and missing_evidence. The two linked publication fixtures passed directly and through pm test. In a disposable checkout with only the workflow change reverted, the single candidate still passed and the explicit delivery case failed with saved PR 42 versus expected PR 43."
